<title>USA: Union Acceptance president recovering.</title>
<headline>Union Acceptance president recovering.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS, Ind. 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Acceptance Corp said on Friday President John Stainbrook is recovering after being hospitalized following a heart attack.</p>
<p>It said Stainbrook, 48, is expected to make a full recovery and return to work in about seven to eight weeks.</p>
<p>In the interim, Jerry Von Deylen, the company's chairman, will handle Stainbrook's day-to-day responsibilities.</p>
<p>Union Acceptance is a specialized finance company that buys and services automobile retail installment sales contracts.</p>
<p>		  ((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
